WEBVTT

00:08.770 --> 00:10.070
<i>This is exhausting.</i>

00:11.390 --> 00:15.190
<i>I never knew using the eye was so tiring.</i>

00:16.020 --> 00:19.880
<i>I've always gotten laughed at because 
I couldn't use the eye very well.</i>

00:22.300 --> 00:27.580
<i>But this time, it'll be a lot 
worse than getting laughed at.</i>

02:07.660 --> 02:08.880
<i>It's no use...</i>

02:08.880 --> 02:10.580
<i>She's closing in.</i>

02:13.110 --> 02:14.110
<i>What the?</i>

02:14.520 --> 02:16.380
<i>There's something chaotic happening.</i>

02:16.380 --> 02:17.400
<i>It's creepy...</i>

02:18.070 --> 02:21.030
<i>I don't think... we need that.</i>

02:21.030 --> 02:22.370
<i>Ow!</i>

02:30.560 --> 02:32.580
Gotcha.

02:33.320 --> 02:41.250
Something so unnecessary ought to be turned 
to stone and broken into pieces.

03:17.090 --> 03:18.700
My pack...

03:19.260 --> 03:21.130
My husband...

03:21.130 --> 03:23.760
My children...

03:28.400 --> 03:30.840
What was I...

03:33.890 --> 03:35.250
My child...

03:35.250 --> 03:38.820
I'm not your child.

03:39.310 --> 03:41.690
Then... my god?

03:41.690 --> 03:42.700
Huh?

03:42.700 --> 03:47.840
You've undone the vile curse 
that was cast upon me.

03:48.680 --> 03:52.290
And so I now remember everything.

03:53.820 --> 03:55.420
I'll be leaving.

03:56.330 --> 03:58.700
Thank you, my god.

04:11.340 --> 04:13.380
I need her to rest.

04:16.590 --> 04:17.850
Lady Philomela!

04:18.520 --> 04:21.600
Her body's begun disintegrating.

04:26.270 --> 04:30.220
I will return what I've been entrusted with.

04:35.310 --> 04:38.370
Detaching the soul from the body?

04:38.680 --> 04:45.030
Yes. I suspect that by severing your soul 
from your body and storing it elsewhere,

04:45.030 --> 04:49.540
you will be able to go 
unnoticed by that mage.

04:50.150 --> 04:50.860
I see.

05:12.370 --> 05:15.820
Even with her soul, her body 
continues to collapse.

05:18.740 --> 05:20.330
Why...

05:21.410 --> 05:25.630
I was born only for this child.

05:26.400 --> 05:27.730
So, why do I...

05:30.710 --> 05:33.700
The same scent as mine.

05:41.080 --> 05:42.810
This is Philomela's scent.

05:42.810 --> 05:44.280
I'm certain of it.

05:45.080 --> 05:47.040
There's no one here.

05:47.280 --> 05:51.570
You'd think there'd always be someone 
around in a mansion this big.

05:51.570 --> 05:52.980
Yeah...

05:53.540 --> 05:59.490
She may have drawn most of
 the humans into the fray.

06:00.190 --> 06:03.670
She's the master of the turmoil of war.

06:04.080 --> 06:05.730
Who is she?

06:05.730 --> 06:08.510
She's what's become of an ancient god.

06:09.280 --> 06:10.260
A god...

06:10.960 --> 06:13.800
Hey, what are you two talking about—

06:17.530 --> 06:20.140
Alcyone-san.

06:20.140 --> 06:21.430
Where is she?

06:21.430 --> 06:24.500
Are you looking for Lady Philomela?

06:24.500 --> 06:26.610
Why else would we be here?

06:27.020 --> 06:29.470
You don't seek the whereabouts
of the magic book?

06:30.320 --> 06:32.140
That isn't a priority.

06:32.620 --> 06:35.540
We're here because we don't 
want Philomela to die.

06:37.390 --> 06:39.770
Come to the office on the second floor.

06:39.770 --> 06:41.750
But only the children.

06:42.150 --> 06:44.440
I ask that <i>you</i> remain here.

06:45.160 --> 06:46.940
Why just me?

06:46.940 --> 06:51.400
You aren't thinking of her, are you?

06:55.180 --> 06:57.710
Chise, I'll see you ahead.

06:59.020 --> 07:00.890
I'll catch up to you soon enough.

07:09.380 --> 07:10.470
That's the room!

07:14.210 --> 07:15.250
Philomela!

07:20.630 --> 07:23.780
<i>The protective amulet's really working.</i>

07:23.780 --> 07:24.980
More...

07:25.700 --> 07:26.860
Philomela!

07:29.800 --> 07:30.550
Chise!

07:36.760 --> 07:39.380
Don't touch my face!

07:39.380 --> 07:40.920
Thanks, Isaac.

07:41.890 --> 07:42.930
Lucy...

07:43.280 --> 07:44.290
Lucy?

07:45.660 --> 07:48.160
What is this?

07:48.160 --> 07:49.190
Lucy!

07:57.270 --> 07:58.870
Explain!

08:00.830 --> 08:01.910
I'm...

08:02.340 --> 08:03.620
I'm sorry.

08:04.100 --> 08:05.200
I'm sorry.

08:06.720 --> 08:08.520
I don't want apologies!

08:08.520 --> 08:10.470
I'm telling you to <i>explain</i> it!

08:11.360 --> 08:14.190
You took everything from me,

08:14.190 --> 08:17.430
and yet you act like you're 
some oblivious victim.

08:17.430 --> 08:20.220
You don't get to be so scared!

08:24.280 --> 08:25.580
But...

08:25.580 --> 08:30.190
But that was all I was ever allowed to do!

08:30.450 --> 08:32.850
Nothing I did was ever enough!

08:33.270 --> 08:35.600
Everything I did was worthless!

08:35.600 --> 08:37.370
A failure!

08:37.810 --> 08:42.780
I'd get scolded and hit and locked up...

08:44.150 --> 08:47.920
I was worried she would mess with my head.

08:48.370 --> 08:49.550
I was scared.

08:49.950 --> 08:51.100
I was so scared.

08:51.570 --> 08:53.810
All I could do was apologize.

08:54.520 --> 08:58.040
But if that's not enough anymore,

08:59.350 --> 09:02.770
what am I supposed to do?!

09:04.640 --> 09:07.080
Please... tell me...

09:08.320 --> 09:12.370
If you really think I'm 
that guilty, then tell me!

09:14.910 --> 09:15.530
Chise!

09:19.000 --> 09:19.930
Okay.

09:32.010 --> 09:33.350
Magic power...

09:33.350 --> 09:34.420
Overflowing...

09:35.520 --> 09:36.890
Why?

09:37.440 --> 09:38.750
Why?

09:53.220 --> 09:54.210
Chise.

09:57.060 --> 09:59.620
<i>What is this place?</i>

10:06.770 --> 10:08.070
Are you all right?

10:08.940 --> 10:11.250
Looks like you've been broken into bits.

10:11.750 --> 10:15.210
Let's pick up your pieces as 
we look for the other two.

10:15.760 --> 10:16.950
<i>Who are you?</i>

10:17.860 --> 10:19.370
I'm Chise.

10:19.980 --> 10:23.010
You're Philomela.

10:28.080 --> 10:29.710
Found a piece.

10:30.260 --> 10:32.090
Let's keep going.

10:34.530 --> 10:37.980
Are we at school?

10:50.630 --> 10:52.540
Hey, what's that?

10:58.810 --> 11:02.120
Rian and I used to play with this a lot.

11:03.510 --> 11:05.670
Rian and I are relatives.

11:05.670 --> 11:07.380
We used to play together sometimes.

11:07.980 --> 11:10.710
He's never been good at this kind of thing.

11:11.700 --> 11:13.370
I can see that.

11:14.600 --> 11:16.620
I was better at it.

11:17.730 --> 11:21.610
But Grandmother never praised me for it.

11:31.480 --> 11:33.250
What about this place?

11:38.800 --> 11:43.280
Whenever I disobeyed, 
I'd get locked in here forever.

11:43.820 --> 11:52.080
I think this was when I couldn't memorize 
the book I was supposed to in time.

11:52.960 --> 11:54.080
Yeah?

11:54.560 --> 11:58.070
It's dark and cold and barren here.

11:58.070 --> 11:59.740
What a terrible place.

12:01.000 --> 12:06.150
Oh, but after this, 
she'd just leave me here.

12:06.150 --> 12:08.670
She wouldn't say anything horrible to me.

12:08.670 --> 12:09.670
So...

12:10.520 --> 12:12.910
But you were scared anyway, weren't you?

12:15.210 --> 12:15.980
Yeah.

12:16.430 --> 12:17.710
I was.

12:23.910 --> 12:26.230
How about this one?

12:28.930 --> 12:31.340
She's so creepy.

12:31.340 --> 12:32.430
And gloomy.

12:32.430 --> 12:35.630
Hatori went and talked to 
someone from Class B.

12:35.630 --> 12:37.620
What? No way.

12:37.620 --> 12:38.630
Horrible.

12:38.630 --> 12:40.140
I bet she's cursed.

12:45.090 --> 12:46.280
Wrong one.

12:46.280 --> 12:48.100
That was a piece of me.

12:48.100 --> 12:50.060
I guess we got a bit mixed up.

12:51.780 --> 12:53.050
Mixed up?

12:54.010 --> 12:58.420
I end up inside people's dreams 
and memories and stuff.

12:58.420 --> 13:00.740
This happens all the time.

13:02.590 --> 13:04.120
Really?

13:12.150 --> 13:13.570
It's a photo.

13:18.510 --> 13:23.820
I don't know my father's 
nor my mother's faces.

13:24.310 --> 13:27.320
Grandmother won't show me their photos.

13:27.320 --> 13:30.290
I don't even know if she has any.

13:30.730 --> 13:32.030
Yeah?

13:33.280 --> 13:38.600
I've never seen my dad's or 
my mom's photos, either.

13:38.600 --> 13:40.660
Mom died.

13:49.970 --> 13:50.950
Let's go.

13:54.820 --> 13:58.400
<i>The mistress is always in 
a bad mood, thanks to her.</i>

13:59.240 --> 14:01.900
<i>She's such a bother.</i>

14:01.900 --> 14:03.910
<i>I wish she'd just disappear.</i>

14:05.530 --> 14:08.230
<i>Ms. Lizbeth is waiting in her office.</i>

14:08.910 --> 14:11.880
<i>She obviously doesn't think 
of her as her grandchild.</i>

14:12.790 --> 14:14.570
<i>She's as cowardly as ever.</i>

14:13.530 --> 14:15.970
<i>Just who does she take after, anyway?</i>

14:17.550 --> 14:20.510
<i>I can't believe Lizbeth 
hasn't abandoned her yet.</i>

14:20.510 --> 14:23.860
<i>How could you screw up something so simple?</i>

14:31.330 --> 14:34.450
We got all the pieces that you lost.

14:35.750 --> 14:36.550
Yeah.

14:40.040 --> 14:43.820
Was there a lot that was scary for you, too?

14:43.820 --> 14:45.830
Yeah, there was.

14:46.320 --> 14:48.360
Scary and lonely.

14:48.670 --> 14:50.690
You just want it to fly away.

14:55.430 --> 14:58.500
Why did you pick up my pieces?

14:59.120 --> 15:02.250
I haven't done anything for you.

15:02.750 --> 15:06.230
In fact, I tried to kill you.

15:07.510 --> 15:12.160
I've been picked up by a lot of people, too.

15:13.180 --> 15:16.220
Piece by piece.

15:17.530 --> 15:23.770
But the truth is, you have 
the same eyes that I used to.

15:24.650 --> 15:27.720
So I think I'm wanting to help 
my past self by helping you.

15:29.880 --> 15:35.580
Sorry I can't tell you I wanted 
to help you specifically.

15:36.250 --> 15:41.370
Even if you told me it was for 
my sake, I wouldn't believe you.

15:42.190 --> 15:48.110
If I'd heard that, I'd want 
to go somewhere far away.

15:50.300 --> 15:51.480
You can.

15:52.080 --> 15:53.240
I can't.

15:53.630 --> 15:56.740
I'm not allowed to.

15:57.450 --> 15:58.300
Do you want to go?

15:59.090 --> 16:01.080
Or do you want to stay?

16:01.850 --> 16:03.390
I don't know.

16:03.390 --> 16:05.300
I'll help you until you do.

16:05.810 --> 16:08.750
So let's keep picking up pieces.

16:07.980 --> 16:09.990
<b>Art Room</b>

16:13.920 --> 16:15.320
Someone's there.

16:16.610 --> 16:18.300
I can't take it anymore.

16:18.300 --> 16:21.050
Everyone keeps comparing me 
to my sister and Rian.

16:21.050 --> 16:24.060
No one expects anything of me.

16:26.380 --> 16:30.260
Why was I born to this family?

16:38.060 --> 16:39.260
Isaac.

16:40.710 --> 16:42.350
Philomela.

16:43.710 --> 16:45.360
Remember us now?

16:45.360 --> 16:47.230
Y-Yeah.

16:47.230 --> 16:49.710
That was embarrassing.

16:49.710 --> 16:50.520
Was it?

16:50.520 --> 16:53.910
I mean, guys shouldn't cry, right?

16:53.910 --> 16:56.190
I... I don't know.

16:56.190 --> 16:57.810
I'd never thought about that.

16:59.410 --> 17:02.290
<b>Library</b>

17:00.510 --> 17:02.280
Now we're just looking for Lucy.

17:02.280 --> 17:04.150
Why the library?

17:02.290 --> 17:08.460
<b>Library</b>

17:04.150 --> 17:06.640
Lucy's studious.

17:11.240 --> 17:13.170
Here, Philomela.

17:13.170 --> 17:14.140
I think this is yours.

17:16.500 --> 17:18.230
Well, let's go.

17:20.770 --> 17:22.930
Cobwebs everywhere.

17:22.930 --> 17:24.430
Can we still go in?

17:24.430 --> 17:25.690
I don't know.

17:28.930 --> 17:30.280
Ow!

17:30.690 --> 17:31.740
Huh?

17:31.740 --> 17:32.780
Lucy?

17:32.780 --> 17:35.010
Were you looking for us?

17:35.010 --> 17:36.480
Obviously!

17:37.140 --> 17:41.960
Why should I just sit in 
here and keep crying?

17:42.260 --> 17:43.610
You were crying?

17:43.610 --> 17:44.990
You were crying.

17:44.990 --> 17:45.990
Shut up!

17:46.310 --> 17:49.660
So much that I can't forget 
even though I want to.

17:49.660 --> 17:52.610
Making yourself sad about 
the past is just miserable.

17:53.230 --> 17:55.770
So I wanna get mad!

17:55.770 --> 17:58.210
I want something to change.

17:58.210 --> 17:59.310
That way...

18:03.290 --> 18:05.530
I won't have to stand still.

18:09.700 --> 18:12.240
I saw you get angry earlier, too.

18:12.760 --> 18:15.520
So why don't you stop whining,

18:15.520 --> 18:19.320
and run away, or do something, 
or say whatever you want?!

18:19.320 --> 18:20.250
Idiot!

18:22.880 --> 18:23.710
Here.

18:26.780 --> 18:30.710
<i>It's time that you get used to it, too.</i>

18:31.150 --> 18:35.810
<i>Follow these people and observe carefully.</i>

18:37.120 --> 18:38.040
No.

18:39.470 --> 18:44.580
<i>May the night forever protect you.</i>

18:45.060 --> 18:46.050
No!

18:46.050 --> 18:47.150
Stop!

18:47.150 --> 18:48.400
Make it stop!

18:49.490 --> 18:52.410
<i>They didn't kill the youngest daughter?</i>

18:52.990 --> 18:56.170
<i>Perhaps they were thinking 
of their own children.</i>

18:56.640 --> 18:58.140
<i>Well, all right.</i>

18:58.140 --> 18:59.990
<i>We got the spiders.</i>

19:00.440 --> 19:02.260
Spiders...?

19:02.860 --> 19:08.030
<i>Philomela, assassination is 
one of this family's duties.</i>

19:06.660 --> 19:08.030
Don't watch!

19:08.790 --> 19:11.110
<i>I have a gift for you.</i>

19:11.110 --> 19:14.730
<i>Should you succeed in using this book</i>

19:14.730 --> 19:17.870
<i>to gather magic power 
from plenty of sorcerers,</i>

19:17.870 --> 19:24.970
<i>I will be able to bring Adam—your father—
and your mother back from the dead.</i>

19:24.970 --> 19:28.020
<i>Now, it's been a long time coming.</i>

19:28.020 --> 19:30.800
<i>Find sacrifices from within the College.</i>

19:33.230 --> 19:35.570
<i>You can do it.</i>

19:36.230 --> 19:39.070
<i>I know I've been strict with you,</i>

19:39.070 --> 19:42.490
<i>but that was always with your 
best interests in mind.</i>

19:43.060 --> 19:47.480
<i>You're a good, capable girl, Philomela.</i>

19:48.340 --> 19:51.530
<i>I can trust you to do it, can't I?</i>

19:51.530 --> 19:52.950
Stop it!

19:56.400 --> 19:57.850
It was you.

19:58.630 --> 20:00.570
You're the one who was there that day.

20:02.800 --> 20:05.610
Why did you kill my family?!

20:06.130 --> 20:07.190
I don't know!

20:07.190 --> 20:08.510
You obviously do!

20:07.950 --> 20:11.530
I was never given the <i>right</i> to know!

20:11.530 --> 20:16.640
Or, what? Should I have told you 
that I was there back then?!

20:16.640 --> 20:20.570
Should I have said sorry 
I couldn't stop them?!

20:20.570 --> 20:21.760
I never...

20:22.020 --> 20:24.620
I <i>never</i> could have done
 anything like that!

20:26.440 --> 20:29.750
Tell me what I could have done.

20:30.270 --> 20:33.360
What could I have done at the time?

20:37.700 --> 20:40.580
No one can give you an answer.

20:41.730 --> 20:44.820
You could just make up anything.

20:45.570 --> 20:49.190
No one can help anyone's past.

20:49.800 --> 20:53.250
But you're allowed to speak up now.

20:53.760 --> 20:55.120
Say what you want.

20:55.120 --> 20:56.630
What you don't want done to you.

20:57.070 --> 20:59.060
What you want others to do for you.

21:00.500 --> 21:01.750
That way...

21:03.120 --> 21:07.780
Someone who wants to help 
you can give you a hand.

21:10.930 --> 21:11.860
I have no one!

21:12.490 --> 21:13.950
I have no one like that!

21:13.950 --> 21:18.400
Even if you don't, I want you to shout

21:18.400 --> 21:20.370
if you want something to change.

21:20.770 --> 21:26.860
I wish help would come even 
without you having to shout or cry.

21:29.250 --> 21:33.530
But that's not the way the world works.

21:34.350 --> 21:37.000
Friends and enemies walk amongst each other,

21:37.530 --> 21:40.390
and all you can do is to 
shout for what you want.

21:42.310 --> 21:44.470
What exactly do you want?

21:45.240 --> 21:46.510
What's your wish?

21:49.740 --> 21:51.510
I...

22:01.690 --> 22:02.420
H...

22:03.590 --> 22:05.360
Help me.

22:09.900 --> 22:12.060
Is that really what you want?

22:15.320 --> 22:16.220
Philomela!
